{
  "tema": 9284,
  "slug": "preterito-experiencias",
  "titulo": "The preterite for experiences",
  "subtitulo": "¿Alguna vez probaste los chapulines?",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "In Mexico the preterite is the usual tense for life experiences: ¿alguna vez fuiste a Cancún?, nunca comí chapulines, fui dos veces. The present perfect (¿has ido…?) is also correct, but less common.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To ask or talk about **experiences** (_have you ever…?_, _I've never…_, _I've been there twice_), Mexican Spanish usually uses the **preterite**, where English uses the present perfect."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "English",
            "Mexican Spanish"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "_Have you ever been to Cancún?_",
              "¿Alguna vez fuiste a Cancún?"
            ],
            [
              "_I've never eaten chapulines._",
              "Nunca comí chapulines."
            ],
            [
              "_I've been to Oaxaca twice._",
              "Fui a Oaxaca dos veces."
            ],
            [
              "_I've already seen that movie._",
              "Ya vi esa película."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Key words: **alguna vez** (_ever_), **nunca** (_never_), **ya** (_already_), **una vez, dos veces** (_once, twice_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The present perfect (**¿Alguna vez has ido a Cancún?**) is also correct and you'll hear it, but the preterite sounds more natural in Mexico."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: in Mexico your past is closed. Even your whole life so far fits in the preterite."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Alguna vez ==surfeaste== en Todos Santos?",
              "en": "Have you ever surfed in Todos Santos?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Nunca ==comí== chapulines.",
              "en": "I've never eaten grasshoppers."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Fui== a Oaxaca dos veces.",
              "en": "I've been to Oaxaca twice."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ya ==viste== la nueva temporada?",
              "en": "Have you seen the new season yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermana nunca ==se subió== a un avión.",
              "en": "My sister has never been on a plane."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Alguna vez ==competiste== en un torneo de jiu-jitsu? —Sí, una vez.",
              "en": "Have you ever competed in a jiu-jitsu tournament? —Yes, once."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nunca ==tuve== perro.",
              "en": "I've never had a dog."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ya ==leí== todos los libros de esa serie.",
              "en": "I've already read all the books in that series."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
